2. Cyclicity supplies the missing premise
----------------------------------------

Suppose H<=G contains distinct commuting involutions s,t. Suppose their
common positive space is a nondegenerate line L=F11*v, and put
p=(I+s)(I+t)/4. Then p lies in F11[H] and is the orthogonal rank-one
projector onto L. More generally, either sign may be recorded in this
formula if the corresponding joint sign space is a nondegenerate line.
All projector and sign-space premises must concern actual elements of H.

If span(v*H)=V, the retained elementary argument 50141b46 gives
F11[H]=End_F11(V). For completeness, choose a cyclic basis w_i=v*h_i.
For right row actions,

 x*(h_i^-1*p*h_j) = B(x,w_i)/B(v,v) * w_j.

The seven functionals B(-,w_i)/B(v,v) form a basis of V*, so these49
rank-one operators span End(V). They belong to F11[H]. In particular H
is irreducible: a subspace invariant under H is invariant under its full
matrix algebra and hence is zero or V. Thus H has no invariant line.

